From: Sayzal28 <Sayzal28@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 16:33:05 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/6] Studio stage: no blink when changing hair; the last drawn
 look stays until the new one is drawn.

The hair swap still blinked in two ways: a swapped-in picture could paint empty while it decoded, and a first hair on a bald
character (one picture -> clothes + hair layers, and back for Bald) hid the character and faded it back in.

- The new clothes + hair pair is decoded off screen before it replaces the old one.
- The stage keeps the look it last drew, out of sight and already loaded; while a new look is still loading, that look is
  shown on top and the new pictures wait hidden, then take over in one frame with no fade (at most 4 s). A look counts as
  drawn only once each of its pictures has loaded. The first appearance of a page still fades in as before.

Checked in the local Studio frame by frame (bald -> hair, hair -> hair, hair -> Bald, Bald -> hair): every frame shows a
loaded picture, never hidden or blank; each change is one swap after 0.1-0.3 s.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../src/components/ExperiencePreview.svelte   | 84 +++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 78 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/packages/experience-studio/src/components/ExperiencePreview.svelte b/packages/experience-studio/src/components/ExperiencePreview.svelte
index 0218542..1e4fd6c 100644
--- a/packages/experience-studio/src/components/ExperiencePreview.svelte
+++ b/packages/experience-studio/src/components/ExperiencePreview.svelte
@@ -1,4 +1,5 @@
